0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;font-family:'Helvetica Neue', Arial, Helvetica, 'Nimbus Sans L', sans-serif;color:rgb(119,119,119);font-size:12px;\"><span class=\"meta-prep meta-prep-author\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\">Posted on</span> <a href=\"http://www.radia.fm/?p=2347\" title=\"4:12 am\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(119,119,119);\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span class=\"entry-date\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\">2013/03/11</span></a> <span class=\"meta-sep\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\">by</span> <span class=\"author vcard\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\"><a class=\"url fn n\" href=\"http://www.radia.fm/?author=5\" title=\"View all posts by fst\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(119,119,119);\" rel=\"nofollow\">fst</a></span></div><div class=\"entry-content\" style=\"background:rgb(255,255,255);border:0px;margin:0px;padding:12px 0px 0px;vertical-align:baseline;clear:both;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Georgia, 'Bitstream Charter', serif;font-size:13.8px;\"><p style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px 0px 24px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\"><a href=\"http://karlender.net/wp-content/uploads/2013/03/P1013585.jpg\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(116,51,153);\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img class=\"size-medium wp-image-3221 alignleft\" src=\"//web.archive.org/web/2im_/http://karlender.net/wp-content/uploads/2013/03/P1013585-300x224.jpg\" alt=\"Radia #415\" style=\"background:transparent;border:none;margin:4px 24px 12px 0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;float:left;height:auto;\" height=\"224\" width=\"300\" /></a>“What is Radio?” – To find answers to this question we immersed ourselves deeply in the world of radio – poetic spoken atmosphere together with a cacophony of thoughts about historical moments in radio-periods were the result. In nearly every person’s life radio plays a major role. But what radio is to the individual mostly differs from what it is for the masses. We guide you with surrounding sounds, voices, words, languages, music and silence through the fascinating and diverse world of radio. You just have to listen.</p><p style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px 0px 24px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\">Producers: Maria Herold & Özge Dayan Mair</p><p style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px 0px 24px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\">Many thanks to the users from <a href=\"http://freesounds.org/\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(116,51,153);\" rel=\"nofollow\">freesounds.org</a>, Tobias Dankl for sound sceneries and the accordion player from Karlsplatz.</p><p style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px 0px 24px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;\">Links: <a href=\"http://kakophoniedergedanken.tumblr.com/\" style=\"background:transparent;border:0px;margin:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(116,51,153);\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://kakophoniedergedanken.tumblr.com/</a></p></div>","licenseurl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/3.0/","radiaseason":"30","scanner":"Internet Archive HTML5 Uploader 1.6.3","subject":"radio art;Radia;Orange 94.0","title":"Show 0415: What is Radio? by Özge Dayan Mair, Maria Herold (Orange 94.0)","publicdate":"2016-11-27 23:11:34","uploader":"radia.fm@gmail.com","addeddate":"2016-11-27 23:11:34","year":"2013","backup_location":"ia906301_31","external_metadata_update":"2019-04-13T10:21:32Z"},"server":"ia801902.us.archive.org","uniq":1661940067,"workable_servers":["ia801902.us.archive.org","ia601902.us.archive.org"]}